s time around for some  reason they come out with two different  models the 6.3 inch and the 6.8 inch  display now on paper you take a look at  the note 10 and you think hmm this is a  bit of an inferior phone when  compared to the no 10 plus it lacks  quite a few qualities that may be of  interest to you but if you're using a  note 10 just for the s-pen and you've  usually found it a little bit  uncomfortable and a little bit too big  well the 6.3 model the note 10 might  actually be perfect for you in this case  so unlike most sampling devices it  actually comes out in a spectrum of  different colors to suit your needs and  your desires for me I'm a pretty  standard guy I like my things to come in  black hence the time so I wouldn't be  choosing anything outside the norm so  the note 10 comes in a variety of five  different colors it comes in the aura  glow which I'm sure you guys have  already seen it reflect light and  creates such a unique little experience  in this almost silver kind of mirror  finish it comes in a black a standard  white and also a red and a pink so these  are a little bit different from your  usual whites and your blacks and right  now in Australia if you do jump online  well you can only buy your aura glow and  the black model I'm not sure if they're  going to announce the other colors or if  they're going to be specific to  different carriers which is more than  likely going to be the case but at the  moment it is raw glow and black it's  very similar with a note 10 plus and  with the exception that it doesn't come  in the pink in the red it comes in this  unique blue color as the fourth option a  couple of things to note if you're  already a Samsung user and it's quite  important because it means you're going  to have to retrain your brain to use  this phone is a simple fact that Samsung  has moved the power button from the  right hand side to the left hand side  where originally the little Bigsby  button used to be so now the big big  button is a multi-purpose button which  actually can be remapped to completely  take out a big speak which is great by  default it's set to a single tap to  unlock the phone and wake the phone any  longer than a single tap it  automatically activates big speed and by  holding down a button it does nothing by  default if you want to remap the button  then obviously you can have it as power  on and long press for complete power off  otherwise to shut down the phone it's no  longer available by pressing down the  Bigsby button or the home button you  actually have to swipe down from the top  the menu and powered down like that the  second feature to note which has kind of  been brushed under the carpet is the  simple fact that they've removed the  headphone jack now this is a huge deal  for Samsung because they haven't removed  the headphone jack in any flagship model  to date now this is also a cheeky little  upselling marketing tactic by Samsung it  means they're going to tribe up sell you  their Samsung Galaxy buds now a little  bit harder than they had done in the  past okay so let's talk a little bit  about the note tens features and then  we're going to talk about in the tens  plus advantages and additional features  so both phones by standard come with a  minimum of twenty five watt fast  charging capabilities the note 10 plus  however you can get a 45 watt  supercharger for an additional cost now  if you're unsure how much more power  this is from your current phone well the  Samsung S 9 and the s10 are using  something like a 15 to an 18 watt power  supply to get there fast charges even  though the battery is significantly  bigger on the note 10 it means you're  going to get a quicker charge with a  standard 25 watt charge and almost  having them out of time when you're  using the supercharger 45 watt charging  being the note series one of the key  features for this flagship is the s-pen  now the S Pen has gotten a complete new  upgrade again from the last year's model  it now comes in a unibody design the S  Pen has also come with some additional  updated features and some gesture  controls built into the unibody design  so now if you have your phone for  example set up on a tripod like I have  my camera here today you can actually  use it to record yourself or record  somebody else from a distance and just  use the s-pen like a magic wand really  to control the device from a distance so  if you want to switch between video mode  live video mode photo mode or anything  in the Samsung menu you can literally  just use the s-pen to swipe across left  and right and go between the menus you  can also flick it up to reverse the  camera and use the opposite camera that  you're using and flick it down then to  bring it back to the selfie mode so I  don't really know how much of  advantages is going to be everybody but  I can definitely see it as a  particularly use for some particular  people for example if you start your  YouTube channel and you don't have  enough to invest in a mirrorless camera  or a DSLR and a brand new flagship  smartphone but you need one to do the  job well the note 10 might be the  perfect device for you you could easily  have this triple camera design set up on  your tripod and get some incredible  content whilst also not having to worry  about anything while changing the  settings now sampling talked quite  heavily about the fact that they're  increasing the capabilities of video  mode so smart phones nowadays really  take amazing images and we're all very  aware of that fact but we know they  still are lacking a little bit in the  video department well Samsung has come  out blatantly and said that it is now  gone from a pro camera to a pro video as  well and this is exciting for somebody  like me especially the simple fact that  they announce super steady mode in the  Samsung Note 10 plus so the comparison  that they gave of the note 9 and the  note 10 plus is actually incredible to  watch they've used AI technology to  increase the stability and to actually  predict the different types of movements  that you might be making to create this  super steady mode now most action camera  companies actually bring this technology  into their cameras way way before this  smartphone was even announced whilst  other companies like Canon and Sony with  a DSLR and mirrorless cameras are still  actually lacking quite a little bit in  this department but that's again the  amount of image quality and the  megapixels you are getting out of a  proper DSLR or mirrorless versus your  smartphone having said that I personally  don't think it's going to be too long  before we can completely remove our  mirrorless cameras and just rely heavily  on our smart phones it might take a  little bit of time for the industry  especially as amateurs try to create  video content and photo content as a  business using a smart phone to adjust  but I think as a society we are going to  get there very quickly and our smart  phones are going to be even more power  and they are right now now a feature  that is unique to the Samsung Note 10  plus is live Bokke mode so if you've  used a new flagship phone by Samsung or  even by Apple you know that in the  settings when you're taking a photo you  can blurt out a whole background and  have a really nice bokeh what you  haven't been able to do in the past is  actually implement this feature into  live video mode using this in video mode  is usually specifically limited to very  expensive video equipment  now that professional-grade technology  has been brought down to consumer level  which is again very exciting news for  everybody that loves take as much as I  do now there is one feature in the note  10 plus that I would happily upgrade  whatever phone I was holding it in time  for so both phones come with a standard  12 megapixel camera the ultra wired 16  megapixel camera and the 12 megapixel  telephoto but the note 10 plus comes  with an additional depth sensing camera  so if you have no idea what a depth  sensing camera is it's the same  technology that they use with facial  recognition in unlocking your smart  phone today however they've gone ahead  advanced the technology to make it even  more useful to the consumer so if you  activate the depth sensing camera on the  no 10 plus you can actually orbit around  an object and the phone will try and  find all the different articulations and  understand what that object looks like  in its entirety example of this  technology is somebody on the  International Space Station could  potentially have one of these phones as  their key tools up there and they could  scan different wrenches different tools  3d print them on the space station and  never need a manufacturing plant or even  need somebody from the earth down below  now in all honesty this is a little bit  of a gimmicky feature and not everybody  we use it especially if you don't have a  3d printer or if you're doing animations  and video but it is an incredibly cool  feature to have and something that's  exciting to see in technology today now  I hope I've covered everything about the  brand new Samsung Note 10 and the no 10  plus if you guys looking at pre-ordering  drop a comment down below let me know  what color you're looking at  pre-ordering because I'll probably be  joy  sometimes so thanks very much for  watching the video guys if you haven't  subscribed already smash that subscribe  button  20:19 style and as always I'll see you  next Monday

